{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1506074360,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzMTQwNTQ0Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1826#issuecomment-331405443"},"message":"There might have been another reason: The remote testrepo on github https://github.com/datalad/testrepo--basic--r1\nThe `test-annex.dat` points to `test.dat` (as in the local case mentioned above), therefore we can have that annex on github. Now, that the `BasicAnnexTestRepo` (as of PR #1845 ) changed and has its own content for `test-annex.dat` the one on github is invalid and can't easily be replaced with the new one.\n\nNot testing with a remote repository at all is not an option, I think. So we need to come up with a solution. For now I'll simply disable the flavor `'network'` for it, but we need a replacement. To a certain extend, this about the entire setup of test repositories.\nCan we have test repositories/datasets on datalad.org?\n\nI'd currently vote in favor of an approach to testrepositories where we have a bunch of them remotely available. Furthermore I'd throw away all of the local efforts to build them. Instead they would need to be cloned. They local building was meant to allow for tests to run without a network connection. We can do this by having a non-temporary place to keep those clones, so you need to download them only once. This location should be protected in the sense, that no test can ever mess with those \"original\" clones. Tests would still run on temporary clones from the protected ones.\nQuestion remains how (and when) to get them and where exactly they should reside.\n  - automatically (try to) get them when tests are started\n  - have dedicated command\n  - ...?\n\nWhat about possible updates or new additional ones?\nAny suggestions or concerns, @yarikoptic , @mih ?\n\nEdit:\nAlternatively we could have a shell script to locally create testrepos. It would use datalad's python API to retrieve the config for location but otherwise do it without using datalad. This might be better than depending on a certain remote location being available.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1577886956,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3MDA1NTA5NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1826#issuecomment-570055094"},"message":"I am closing this old issue. We are currently generating a file URL pointing to an external tmp location.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1577886956,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MjkxNjUyNTMzNA=="},"status":2}]}